<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108414" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποθετ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hypothetical,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Epict.</u>
					1.7.22
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Asp.
				<u>in EN</u>
				18.27
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχῆμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					186.27
				</span></i>
			; distd. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκθετικός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.62
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					4.609
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				3.12
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>belonging to the subject,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ἐξήγησις</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				14
			</span></i> init. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>suggestive, hortatory,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Muson.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					17p.91H.
				</span></i>
			
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				<i>by way of suggestion,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demetr.
					<u>Eloc.</u>
					296
				</span></i>
			.</div>
